# Merlin has no .dockerignore and does not need one. Peregrine does: the repo
# working tree is around 692 MB, almost all of it the whisper model and the
# bundled ffmpeg binary, and `COPY . .` would push every byte of that into the
# builder layer on every build. CI builds the image twice (docker-build and
# push-image) for two architectures, so without this file that is roughly
# 2.7 GB of pointless context per run.
#
# The build only needs Go sources, go.mod and go.sum. Everything else here is
# excluded on purpose.

.git
.github
.claude
.gitignore

# Secrets and runtime data must never enter an image layer, even transiently:
# a layer is a permanent, distributable copy.
.env
blocklist.txt
markov.db
markov.db.lock
*.db.tmp
backups/

# The transcription assets, which is the 692 MB.
voicenotes/models/
voicenotes/bin/
voicenotes/audio/

# Build output from a host build, which would otherwise shadow the one the
# builder stage produces.
/bin/
/dist/
peregrine
peregrine.exe

*.log

# Docs are excluded from the build context but deliberately NOT from the prose
# CI job, which runs against the checkout rather than the image.
*.md
LICENSE
docker-compose*.yml
Dockerfile
